  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nNorthwest flow aloft with a large area of surface high pressure\nbuilding southeast across the Great Lakes and Ohio Valley thru the\nweek. This high will offer cooler and dry conditions thru Friday. \nExpect abundant sunshine with pleasant highs in the upper 70s to the\nlower 80s today, slowly warming to the lower and middle 80s Friday.  \nThese readings are close to 5 degrees below normal today and Thursday\nand close to normal Friday. \n\nA system digging southeast in the flow will offer the first threat\nfor showers and thunderstorms late Friday night. Precipitation\nchances look to increase Saturday as the low tracks thru the Ohio\nValley. As this system meanders thru the region precipitation chances\ncontinue Sunday and into early next week.",
